Subject: [Krypton] Let the native toolbar draw extension badges

Chromium paints an extension's badge into its toolbar icon at a fixed size.
Krypton draws the badge natively over the address field's extension icon,
using the same badge metrics as the rest of its chrome. Give the native host
the icon without its badge, and the action whose badge state it draws. Views
toolbar callers keep the badged icon from GetIcon().

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/extensions/extension_action_view_model.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/extensions/extension_action_view_model.cc
@@ -748,6 +748,17 @@
   return GetIconImageSource(web_contents, size);
 }
 
+ui::ImageModel ExtensionActionViewModel::GetIconWithoutBadge(
+    content::WebContents* web_contents,
+    const gfx::Size& size) {
+  if (!ExtensionIsValid()) {
+    return ui::ImageModel();
+  }
+
+  return ui::ImageModel::FromImageSkia(gfx::ImageSkia(
+      GetIconImageSource(web_contents, size, /*include_badge=*/false), size));
+}
